      "section": "P2",
      "question_number": 6,
      "question_text": "6 A student attempts to solve the equation cos x + sin x tan x = 2 sin x − 1 in the range 0 ≤ x ≤ 2π. The student’s attempt is as follows: cos x + sin x tan x = 2 sin x − 1 So cos x − sin x + sin x tan x − sin x = −1 (I) So (sin x − cos x)(tan x − 1) = −1 (II) So sin x − cos x = −1 or tan x − 1 = −1 (III) So (sin x − cos x)2 = 1 or tan x = 0 (IV) So 2 sin x cos x = 0 or tan x = 0 (V) So x = 0, π2 , π, 3π 2 , 2π (VI) Which of the following best describes this attempt?",
      "has_diagram": false,
      "options": {
        "A": "It is completely correct",
        "B": "It is incorrect, and the ﬁrst error occurs on line (I)",
        "C": "It is incorrect, and the ﬁrst error occurs on line (II)",
        "D": "It is incorrect, and the ﬁrst error occurs on line (III)",
        "E": "It is incorrect, and the ﬁrst error is that extra solutions were introduced on line (IV)",
        "F": "It is incorrect, and the ﬁrst error is that extra solutions were introduced on line (V)",
        "G": "It is incorrect, and the ﬁrst error is not eliminating the values where tan x is undeﬁned on line (VI) 8"
      },
      "correct_answer": "D",
      "raw_text": "6   A student attempts to solve the equation\n                                 cos x + sin x tan x = 2 sin x − 1\n    in the range 0 ≤ x ≤ 2π.\n    The student’s attempt is as follows:\n        cos x + sin x tan x = 2 sin x − 1\n        So   cos x − sin x + sin x tan x − sin x = −1                         (I)\n        So   (sin x − cos x)(tan x − 1) = −1                                  (II)\n        So   sin x − cos x = −1 or tan x − 1 = −1                             (III)\n        So   (sin x − cos x)2 = 1 or tan x = 0                                (IV)\n        So   2 sin x cos x = 0 or tan x = 0                                   (V)\n        So   x = 0, π2 , π, 3π\n                             2\n                               , 2π                                           (VI)\n    Which of the following best describes this attempt?\n    A It is completely correct\n    B It is incorrect, and the ﬁrst error occurs on line (I)\n    C It is incorrect, and the ﬁrst error occurs on line (II)\n    D It is incorrect, and the ﬁrst error occurs on line (III)\n    E It is incorrect, and the ﬁrst error is that extra solutions were introduced on\n      line (IV)\n    F It is incorrect, and the ﬁrst error is that extra solutions were introduced on\n      line (V)\n    G It is incorrect, and the ﬁrst error is not eliminating the values where tan x is\n      undeﬁned on line (VI)\n                                               8",
